  <section aria-labelledby="authorization">
    <h2 id="authorization">2. Authorization and responsibilities</h2>
    <p>The operator must use only accounts and information they are authorized to access, review OAuth permissions, and comply with applicable Google policies and the <a href="/mydashboard/privacy/">MyDashboard privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>Messages, calendar changes, and other consequential actions require the operator’s instructions or an explicitly approved automation. The operator is responsible for checking recipients, dates, generated content, and other details before relying on a result.</p>
    <p>Do not submit another person’s credentials, use the integration for spam or unauthorized access, or publish private account content or authentication secrets in this website.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="ai">
    <h2 id="ai">3. AI-assisted output and data handling</h2>
    <p>Generated summaries, suggested replies, and extracted dates can be incomplete or incorrect. They are assistance, not authoritative professional advice or a substitute for reviewing the original information.</p>
    <p>Any AI processing of Google-derived information must follow the privacy policy, Google’s applicable Limited Use requirements, and compatible provider arrangements. A provider’s availability in Hermes does not establish that its default data settings satisfy those requirements.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="availability">
    <h2 id="availability">4. Availability and limitations</h2>
    <p>MyDashboard is provided on a personal, best-effort basis without a promise of uninterrupted service, accuracy, or permanent Google authorization. Network failures, software changes, account settings, quotas, or third-party policies can interrupt access.</p>
    <p>The operator should maintain suitable backups and verify important work. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or responsibilities that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="ending">
    <h2 id="ending">5. Ending use</h2>
    <p>The operator may stop using the integration and revoke its Google authorization at any time through <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google Account connections</a>. Follow the privacy policy’s separate steps to remove previously retained credentials and information.</p>
  </section>
